            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A source of impending divine judgment, hostile invasion, and disaster, often associated with destructive empires like Babylon or Assyria.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Jeremiah 1:14\",\"Jeremiah 4:6\",\"Jeremiah 6:22\",\"Ezekiel 38:15\",\"Joel 2:20\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"The dwelling place of God, the divine council, or the sacred mountain (Mount Zaphon).\",\"basis\":[\"Psalm 48:2\",\"Isaiah 14:13\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A place of cold, darkness, or mysterious forces.\",\"basis\":[\"Job 37:9\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Because invading Mesopotamian armies entered Israel from the north to avoid the Arabian desert, the north became a prophetic metonym for judgment and devastation. In other poetic contexts, the term borrows from Ancient Near Eastern mythology referring to the sacred mountain of the gods (Zaphon), representing divine exaltation.\"}",
